  "calculators": {
    "urn:sbrm:calculator:div7a:at": {
      "label": "Division 7A minimum yearly repayment",
      "route": "/v1/calculators/div7a/at/{period_uri}",
      "supported_periods": [
        "urn:sbrm:period:div7a:fy2025",
        "urn:sbrm:period:div7a:fy2026"
      ],
      "input_schema_ref": "#/components/schemas/Div7aAtInput",
      "request_number_fields": [
        "amalgamated_base",
        "repayments[].amount"
      ],
      "scope_notes": [
        "The provider derives the remaining term from loan_term_years, loan_origination_date and income_year_start_date, with is_first_real_myr_year as an override. The local engine takes the remaining term as an operator assertion and applies the s 109E(6) rounding to it.",
        "The provider returns is_complying and deemed_dividend. Those are the provider's labels for its own arithmetic. They are not a Division 7A determination and must not be mapped onto the local engine's gate verdicts.",
        "Live on 18 September 2026 this route returned statutory_myr 21874.92, shortfall 0.00, total_repayments 22000.00 and benchmark_rate 0.0837 for the fabricated loan in fixtures/example-div7a-request.json, agreeing to the cent with both the local engine and the s 109E(6) formula evaluated independently."
      ],
      "required_decimal_fields": [
        "benchmark_rate",
        "statutory_myr",
        "total_repayments",
        "shortfall"
      ],
      "optional_decimal_fields": [
        "deemed_dividend",
        "interest_accrued"
      ]
    },
    "urn:sbrm:calculator:depreciation:at": {
      "label": "AASB 116 carrying amount at a date",
      "route": "/v1/calculators/depreciation/at/{period_uri}",
      "supported_periods": [
        "urn:sbrm:period:depreciation:unscoped"
      ],
      "input_schema_ref": "#/components/schemas/DepreciationAtInput",
      "request_number_fields": [
        "asset.cost",
        "asset.accounting_useful_life_years",
        "asset.dv_rate_factor"
      ],
      "scope_notes": [
        "Accounting basis only. This is not a Division 40 deduction and the tax figure will not equal it.",
        "basis accepts only the literal \"accounting\"; a pooled asset returns 400 pool_asset_out_of_t6_scope.",
        "The reviewed EventInput uses amount for cost additions and opening balances, and new_useful_life_years for reassessments."
      ],
      "required_decimal_fields": [
        "wdv_at",
        "period_dep_at"
      ],
      "optional_decimal_fields": []
    },
    "urn:sbrm:calculator:depreciation:range": {
      "label": "AASB 116 depreciation over a range",
      "route": "/v1/calculators/depreciation/range/{period_uri}",
      "supported_periods": [
        "urn:sbrm:period:depreciation:unscoped"
      ],
      "input_schema_ref": "#/components/schemas/DepreciationRangeInput",
      "request_number_fields": [
        "asset.cost",
        "asset.accounting_useful_life_years",
        "asset.dv_rate_factor"
      ],
      "scope_notes": [
        "day_count is required on this route and has no default.",
        "The current response must carry cost_additions for initial recognition and additions inside the range, even when it is zero. The adapter checks the movement before accepting the result. Older evidence remains readable.",
        "The reviewed EventInput uses amount for cost additions and opening balances, and new_useful_life_years for reassessments."
      ],
      "required_decimal_fields": [
        "range_dep",
        "opening_wdv",
        "closing_wdv",
        "cost_additions"
      ],
      "optional_decimal_fields": []
    },
    "urn:sbrm:calculator:fbt:car-statutory-formula": {
      "label": "FBT car, statutory formula method",
      "route": "/v1/calculators/{calc_uri}/{period_uri}",
      "supported_periods": [
        "urn:sbrm:period:fbt:fy2026"
      ],
      "input_schema_ref": "#/components/schemas/FBTCarStatutoryFormulaInput",
      "request_number_fields": [
        "baseValue",
        "daysAvailable",
        "accessories",
        "employeeContribution"
      ],
      "scope_notes": [
        "taxable_value is the category taxable value. grossed_up_taxable_value and fbt_payable are derived from it and must never be grossed up again.",
        "fbtType selects the gross-up rate and defaults engine-side to Type 2 when omitted. Type 1 and type 2 classification is a professional judgement about creditable acquisitions, which this adapter requires the caller to establish rather than inheriting the default.",
        "Live on 18 September 2026: a 40000.00 base value available all year with no accessories or employee contribution returned taxable_value 8000.00, grossed_up_taxable_value 15094.40 and fbt_payable 7094.37. Carrying only the category taxable value into austaxcalc.fbt as a Type 2 amount produced the same 15094.40 and 7094.37."
      ],
      "required_decimal_fields": [
        "taxable_value"
      ],
      "optional_decimal_fields": [
        "gross_up_factor",
        "grossed_up_taxable_value",
        "fbt_payable"
      ]
    }
  },
